 "section_summary": "This section contains U.S. State Department records relating to animal husbandry and domestic animals in occupied Japan. The bulk of the material consists of Report No. 30 of the SCAP Natural Resources Section, 'The Livestock Industry of Japan' (April 18, 1946), transmitted with a cover despatch from the U.S. Political Adviser in Tokyo, which provides a comprehensive statistical and administrative review of livestock populations, feed shortages, slaughter, and production across all prefectures from 1926 to 1946. The section concludes with a February 1948 despatch from the Acting Political Adviser concerning dog registration and the Japan Shepherd Dog Association, followed by the misfiled distribution schedule for Report No. 30.",
