   "start_page": 2,
   "summary": "This comprehensive survey by SCAP's Natural Resources Section examines the Japanese livestock industry, compiling detailed population, slaughter, and production figures from 1926 through 1945 across all prefectures for dairy cattle, draft cattle, horses, hogs, sheep, goats, rabbits, and poultry. It analyzes the severe impact of wartime concentrate feed shortages and food scarcity on domestic herds, alongside government breeding and distribution controls. The report outlines the 1946 production outlook, concluding that significant expansion is heavily restricted by limited pasturage and feed supplies.",
   "title": "Report No. 30: The Livestock Industry of Japan",
   "to": "General Headquarters, Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers"
  },
